<title>DENMARK: Danish Dec North Sea gas production unchanged.</title>
<headline>Danish Dec North Sea gas production unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from its North Sea fields was the same 554 million cubic metres in December 1996 as in November of the same year, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    (Million cubic metres)   Dec 96    Nov 96   Dec 95</p>
<p>    Total production	    554	  554	 516</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the third-biggest producer in western Europe after Norway and Britain.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom 45-33-969656</p>
